<Project>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <LangVersion>12.0</LangVersion>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>false</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <InvariantGlobalization>true</InvariantGlobalization>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Version pinning notes. Do NOT bump one of these without checking the other.

    Avalonia and Svg.Skia both surface raw SkiaSharp types, and we draw SVG pictures straight into
    Avalonia's Skia canvas via ISkiaSharpApiLease. If the two resolve to different SkiaSharp majors
    the app compiles fine and then dies at runtime with a TypeLoadException on SKCanvas.

      Avalonia      11.3.19 -> SkiaSharp 2.88.9
      Svg.Skia       4.8.0  -> SkiaSharp 2.88.9   (exact match)

    Known-bad combinations, for whoever tries to upgrade next:
      * Svg.Skia >= 4.9.0 moves to SkiaSharp 3.119.x and breaks against Avalonia 11.3.
      * Avalonia 12.x does pair with Svg.Skia 5.x on SkiaSharp 3.119.x, but its source generators
        require Roslyn 4.14 (.NET 10 SDK). This machine has SDK 8.0.421 / Roslyn 4.11, where the
        generator silently does not run and every x:Name field fails to compile. Moving to
        Avalonia 12 means installing a newer .NET SDK first.
      * Avalonia.Svg.Skia (the wrapper) tops out at SkiaSharp 2.88.x on an Avalonia 11.3 baseline
        but is not published for 12.x at all. We do not use it: all we need is SKSvg -> SKPicture,
        and we custom-draw everything anyway.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <AvaloniaVersion>11.3.19</AvaloniaVersion>
    <SvgSkiaVersion>4.8.0</SvgSkiaVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
